1d:["$","p",null,{"className":"text-base text-[#17202A] font-normal leading-relaxed","children":"One of the most frequent surprises international travelers share when arriving at Colombo Airport is the pacing of Sri Lankan roads. While a 120-kilometer stretch on the Southern Expressway between Colombo and Galle takes just 90 minutes, that same distance winding up into Nuwara Eliya or Ella takes close to 4 to 5 hours. To experience the real Sri Lanka without exhaustion, the secret is clustering your regions intelligently."}]
1e:["$","section","0",{"className":"space-y-4 pt-4 border-t border-[#E8E2D2]/60","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl sm:text-2xl font-extrabold text-[#17202A] tracking-tight","children":"1. The Classic Golden Loop (Culture, Tea, Safari & Coast)"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-[#5B6770] leading-relaxed","children":"For a 7 to 10-day first visit, we almost always recommend moving clockwise: CMB Airport → Cultural Triangle (Sigiriya/Dambulla) → Kandy → Hill Country (Nuwara Eliya or Ella via scenic train) → Yala Safari → Southern Coast (Mirissa/Hikkaduwa) → Colombo. This route keeps transit legs under 3 to 4 hours per day and matches the natural elevation curve of the island."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-[#FBF9F4] p-4 sm:p-5 rounded-2xl border border-[#E8E2D2] flex items-start gap-3 mt-4","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"w-8 h-8 rounded-xl bg-[#E06D53]/15 text-[#E06D53] flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 mt-0.5","children":["$","$L1b",null,{"ref":"$undefined","icon":{"name":"lightbulb","size":24,"node":[["path",{"d":"M15 14c.2-1 .7-1.7 1.5-2.5 1-.9 1.5-2.2 1.5-3.5A6 6 0 0 0 6 8c0 1 .2 2.2 1.5 3.5.7.7 1.3 1.5 1.5 2.5","key":"1gvzjb"}],["path",{"d":"M9 18h6","key":"x1upvd"}],["path",{"d":"M10 22h4","key":"ceow96"}]]},"className":"w-4 h-4"}]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-extrabold text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-[#0C5A70] mb-0.5","children":"Local Chauffeur Secret"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs text-[#5B6770] leading-relaxed","children":"Avoid rushing from Sigiriya to Ella in a single day. Break the journey in Kandy or Nuwara Eliya to allow your senses to adjust to the mountain mist and cooler temperatures."}]]}]]}]]}]
1f:["$","section","1",{"className":"space-y-4 pt-4 border-t border-[#E8E2D2]/60","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl sm:text-2xl font-extrabold text-[#17202A] tracking-tight","children":"2. Demystifying the Dual Monsoons"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-[#5B6770] leading-relaxed","children":"Sri Lanka has two distinct weather seasons, which means there is always sunshine somewhere on the island. From December through April, the south coast (Hikkaduwa, Mirissa, Galle) and western beaches enjoy calm, glassy seas and peak whale-watching weather. From May through September, the east coast (Trincomalee, Passikudah) enjoys calm turquoise waters while the cultural triangle stays warm and dry."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-[#FBF9F4] p-4 sm:p-5 rounded-2xl border border-[#E8E2D2] flex items-start gap-3 mt-4","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"w-8 h-8 rounded-xl bg-[#E06D53]/15 text-[#E06D53] flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 mt-0.5","children":["$","$L1b",null,{"ref":"$undefined","icon":"$1e:props:children:2:props:children:0:props:children:props:icon","className":"w-4 h-4"}]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-extrabold text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-[#0C5A70] mb-0.5","children":"Local Chauffeur Secret"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs text-[#5B6770] leading-relaxed","children":"If you are visiting between May and October, don't write off the hill country! A light mountain mist in Ella often makes the tea plantations look even more magical."}]]}]]}]]}]
20:["$","section","2",{"className":"space-y-4 pt-4 border-t border-[#E8E2D2]/60","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl sm:text-2xl font-extrabold text-[#17202A] tracking-tight","children":"3. Why Private Chauffeured Travel Transforms Your Trip"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-[#5B6770] leading-relaxed","children":"Self-driving rental cars in Sri Lanka can be stressful due to sudden switchbacks, tuk-tuks, and village bus overtaking customs. With your own dedicated local driver, you can look out the window, spot wild peafowls and water monitors, nap between stops, and ask your chauffeur to pull over whenever you spot a roadside fruit stall slicing fresh golden mangoes."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-[#FBF9F4] p-4 sm:p-5 rounded-2xl border border-[#E8E2D2] flex items-start gap-3 mt-4","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"w-8 h-8 rounded-xl bg-[#E06D53]/15 text-[#E06D53] flex items-center justify-center shrink-0 mt-0.5","children":["$","$L1b",null,{"ref":"$undefined","icon":"$1e:props:children:2:props:children:0:props:children:props:icon","className":"w-4 h-4"}]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-extrabold text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-[#0C5A70] mb-0.5","children":"Local Chauffeur Secret"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs text-[#5B6770] leading-relaxed","children":"Ask your chauffeur to take the secondary rural routes through Kurunegala or Wellawaya instead of the congested main truck highways."}]]}]]}]]}]
21:["$","div",null,{"className":"pt-6 border-t border-[#E8E2D2]","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"text-base font-medium text-[#17202A] leading-relaxed","children":"Traveling Sri Lanka is about unhurried moments—stopping for sweet roadside king coconuts, watching children fly kites on the ramparts of Galle Fort, and enjoying warm village welcomes. Let us know your dates, and we'll blueprint your custom route within 24 hours."}]}]
